<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">
<ins></ins>Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Arms Warrior DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar, Naxxramas, Obsidian Sanctum, and Eye of Eternity. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Arms Warrior DPS in Phase 2</h2>While Arms Warrior has a wide variety of stats it can use, we want to mostly focus on the following priority<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - Aim for 8% Hit Rating,</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength - Strength is a Arms Warrior's primary stat, and gives 2 base AP per point of Strength. As one of our strongest stats, this will be our primary stat to look for/<wbr/>gem whenever you are unsure of any other stat to pick up.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Armor Penetration Rating - While this stat may not be very strong early on due to the way ArP rating scales, it becomes increasingly strong as we approach "soft" ArP cap (1260 with an ArP trinket active, due to Battle Stance increasing our ArP by 10%). As such, monitoring your current ArP levels can be important to know when to focus more on obtaining this stat.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - Although our abilities refund rage when avoided, ensuring our casts can't dodge will help our damage quite a lot. However, due to our Overpower ability also being able to proc on dodges, we can afford to remain below Expertise cap when compared to other specs.</div></li></ol>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gearing-options-for-arms-warrior-dps-in-phase-2">Gearing options for Arms Warrior DPS in Phase 2</h4>Arms Warrior has two main gearing options in Phase 2 - A setup using either a Sword, or a Poleaxe configuration. Due to our primary choice in Poleaxe being <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45533/dark-edge-of-depravity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_halberd_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Edge of Depravity</span></a>, with a massive hit budget, any setup using a Sword, despite leaning towards being slightly higher DPS, will inevitably be forced to rely far more on strong hit items, many of which come from difficult and contested 25M HM bosses. In addition. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45533/dark-edge-of-depravity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_halberd_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Edge of Depravity</span></a> is not as contested as Vold'rethar, so it may be a far easier setup to achieve.<div class="pad"></div>
