<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="hands">Hands for Arms Warrior DPS in Phase 2</h3>Hands end up being a very easy slot to worry about when running <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45533/dark-edge-of-depravity">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_halberd_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Edge of Depravity</span></a>. - Tier in the form of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46148/conquerors-siegebreaker-gauntlets">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Siegebreaker Gauntlets</span></a> becomes our hand slot, and will remain that way in almost any setup that you create with this weapon.<br/>
<br/>However, if running a sword configuration, then the extra hit granted from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45444/gloves-of-the-steady-hand">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_48.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gloves of the Steady Hand</span></a> is indispensable, and will be almost required in order to achieve hit caps without running subpar items in other slots.<br/>
<br/>If you are finding yourself unlucky with tier tokens, you can pickup the somewhat unwanted <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45833/bladebreaker-gauntlets">
