<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Arms Warrior DPS in Phase 2</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42987/darkmoon-card-greatness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarotgreatness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Greatness</span></a> maintains its strength in Ulduar, keeping it as a strong option even when confronted with with the boosted trinkets present in this new patch. Of note are both 10M and 25M Algalon trinkets, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46038/dark-matter">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_seedofdestruction.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dark Matter</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45609/comets-trail">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_starfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Comet's Trail</span></a> respectively. All 3 of these trinkets are close to each other, and I recommend simming yourself to figure out how much of an increase each of these items are.<br/>
<br/>However, another factor in the discussion around <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45609/comets-trail">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_starfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Comet's Trail</span></a> is its importance for other classes. Notably, Unholy DK, as well as a couple of other specs, potentially use it for the rest of the game. Just as Melancholy Sabatons were important for us, this trinket is a small upgrade when compared to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42987/darkmoon-card-greatness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarotgreatness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Greatness</span></a> for us, but is a massive increase for your raid.<br/>
<br/>However, the big winner in Ulduar is 100% <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45931/mjolnir-runestone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rune_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mjolnir Runestone</span></a>, from 10M Thorim. This strong ArP focused trinket allows us to "soft cap" ArP, meaning that we reach the cap of 1400 ArP rating during its proc windows. As it is on the standard 45s ICD, this allows us to sync it up neatly with our other trinkets and cooldowns, massively increasing our burst window.<div class="pad"></div>
